## [tx] AFK (idle) detection: a big on-screen 'AFK' title with a randomly rotating humorous subtitle
## [tx] (sub_01..sub_55, one shown at a time, changing every ~45s) plus chat warnings before an
## [tx] optional idle auto-kick. The jokes reference Minecraft trivia and real life — adapt the
## [tx] humor freely, but keep lines short (they render as a screen subtitle) and use official
## [tx] Minecraft names for mobs/items.

jm_at.afk.title=§9§lAFK
jm_at.afk.warn=§e[AFK] You are now marked as AFK.
jm_at.afk.warn_kick=§e[AFK] You will be kicked if you remain idle. Time left: %1$s min.
jm_at.afk.sub_01=Did you fall into the void?
jm_at.afk.sub_02=Hello? Is anyone home?
jm_at.afk.sub_03=Gone to mine IRL?
jm_at.afk.sub_04=Did a Creeper get you in real life?
jm_at.afk.sub_05=Off touching grass?
jm_at.afk.sub_06=Your chair is empty. We miss you.
jm_at.afk.sub_07=You had somewhere to be, apparently.
jm_at.afk.sub_08=Disappeared without a trace...
jm_at.afk.sub_09=Probably on the phone...
jm_at.afk.sub_10=Crafting a sandwich?
jm_at.afk.sub_11=Out there somewhere, living life.
jm_at.afk.sub_12=Off getting a snack. Probably.
jm_at.afk.sub_13=Exploring the fridge biome?
jm_at.afk.sub_14=Last seen heading for the door.
jm_at.afk.sub_15=Did someone steal your controls?
jm_at.afk.sub_16=Out there doing something, presumably.
jm_at.afk.sub_17=Walked away without pausing... classic.
jm_at.afk.sub_18=Probably forgot they were playing.
jm_at.afk.sub_19=Your seat is warm. Come back to it.
jm_at.afk.sub_20=We'll keep the lights on.
jm_at.afk.sub_21=Status: unknown.
jm_at.afk.sub_22=You left the game, but not our hearts.
jm_at.afk.sub_23=Wandering around in the real world, maybe?
jm_at.afk.sub_24=Fell in a ravine?
jm_at.afk.sub_25=Your pickaxe awaits.
jm_at.afk.sub_26=No movement detected. Curious.
jm_at.afk.sub_27=You've got blocks to break!
jm_at.afk.sub_28=You're missing out on all the fun!
jm_at.afk.sub_29=Don't forget to take breaks, but maybe not this long!
jm_at.afk.sub_30=The world is waiting for you.
jm_at.afk.sub_31=You left without saying goodbye...
jm_at.afk.sub_32=Lost in the mines?
jm_at.afk.sub_33=Somewhere without a map.
jm_at.afk.sub_34=Last seen heading toward a ravine.
jm_at.afk.sub_35=Probably just AFK farming, right?
jm_at.afk.sub_36=Busy in the Discord?
jm_at.afk.sub_37=You'll turn up eventually.
jm_at.afk.sub_38=Waiting on you.
jm_at.afk.sub_39=The clock is ticking.
jm_at.afk.sub_40=You've been gone a while now.
jm_at.afk.sub_41=We saved your spot.
jm_at.afk.sub_42=Come back when you're ready. But sooner.
jm_at.afk.sub_43=Taking the scenic route back.
jm_at.afk.sub_44=Did you know?\nCreepers were a pig model gone horribly wrong.\nThanks, Notch.
jm_at.afk.sub_45=Did you know?\nThe Ender Dragon's name is Jean.
jm_at.afk.sub_46=Did you know?\nCats scare away Creepers and Phantoms.
jm_at.afk.sub_47=Did you know?\nYou can fish players with a fishing rod.
jm_at.afk.sub_48=Did you know?\nParrots dance to music.
jm_at.afk.sub_49=Did you know?\nFoxes steal your items. Little orange bandits.
jm_at.afk.sub_50=Did you know?\nLightning turns pigs into Zombified Piglins.
jm_at.afk.sub_51=Did you know?\nAn anvil to the head does damage.\nPhysics works sometimes.
jm_at.afk.sub_52=Did you know?\nDolphins boost your swim speed.
jm_at.afk.sub_53=Did you know?\nTNT used to go off when you punched it.\nBold design choice.
jm_at.afk.sub_54=Did you know?\nA Minecraft day is 20 minutes.\nYou're missing the whole month.
jm_at.afk.sub_55=The block game awaits your return.

