jm_at.cl.help_admin_managed=§c§lClaims are admin-managed on this server.§r
jm_at.cl.help_budget=§9§lYour Budget§r\n• Claims: %1$s/%2$s\n• Area used: %3$s/%4$s chunks\n• Chunks earned per §2%6$s§r min of playtime: §2%5$s§r\n• Starting budget: %7$s chunks  •  Max budget: %8$s chunks
jm_at.cl.help_dims=§9§lDimensions§r\n• Nether: %1$s§r  •  End: %2$s§r
jm_at.cl.help_expand=§9§lExpand & Extend§r\n• §6Expand§r — select a larger area that fully encompasses your claim to grow it in place. Expanding an extended claim will merge it into one rectangle and reset your extensions.\n• §6Extend§r — select an area that borders your claim to attach an extension (up to 2 per claim). Extensions share the same protections and members as the main claim.
jm_at.cl.help_members=§9§lMembers§r\nAdd players to your claim with a role:\n• §lVisitor§r — can enter the claim but cannot interact\n• §lMember§r — can use doors, buttons, and levers\n• §lBuilder§r — full access to build and interact\n• §lCo-owner§r — can manage the claim (add members, change settings, create sub-claims)\n\nMembers can be temporary (15 min to 7 days) or permanent.
jm_at.cl.help_overlap=§9§lWhen land is already claimed§r\nThe menu shows what a selection will do before you confirm. If it §ccan't§r be claimed (it overlaps another claim, you're over budget, or at your claim limit), the reason shows in §cred§r and no Confirm button appears. To use land near an existing claim you can instead §6Expand§r (select fully around your own claim), §6Sub-claim§r (select inside a claim you manage), or pick a clear spot.
jm_at.cl.help_overlap_staff= §7As staff, creating an Admin claim over existing claims will §coverwrite§r (delete) them. You're warned first, except claims marked Owner-Only by another player, which can't be overwritten.§r
jm_at.cl.help_overlap_staff_owner= §7As staff, creating an Admin/Owner-Only claim over existing claims will §coverwrite§r (delete) them. You're warned first, except claims marked Owner-Only by another player, which can't be overwritten.§r
jm_at.cl.help_owner_only=§9§lOwner-Only Claims§r\nAs the Server Owner you can mark a new claim §4Owner-Only§r when confirming it, making it completely private: no other admin or moderator can enter, build, open containers, view or change its settings, expand, or even delete it, and it's hidden from the admin claim lists.
jm_at.cl.help_prot_head=§9§lProtections§r\nNew claims use the server's default protections. You can toggle:
jm_at.cl.help_prot_line=  §2✓§r %1$s
jm_at.cl.help_prot_line_admin=  §6✓§r %1$s §8(admin)§r
jm_at.cl.help_prot_line_admin_only=  §8✗ %1$s (admin only)§r
jm_at.cl.help_ranks=§9§lTrusted Ranks§r\nTrust a server rank to give all players with that rank access to your claim. Each trusted rank has a role (visitor, member, builder, or co-owner) and can be set to expire. Useful for granting access to groups without adding players individually.
jm_at.cl.help_subclaims=§9§lSub-claims§r\nSelect an area inside an existing claim to create a sub-claim with its own protections and members. Up to %1$s sub-claims per claim. Sub-claims can be nested up to two levels deep (e.g. city → district → house).
jm_at.cl.help_tool=§9§lClaim Tool§r\n§l1.§r §2Crouch + Hit§r a block to set §lCorner 1§r.\n§l2.§r §2Crouch + Interact§r on a block to set §lCorner 2§r.\n§l3.§r Open this menu and tap §lConfirm Pending Claim§r.\nA marker appears at each corner you pick so you can see your pending selection before confirming; tap §lCancel Selection§r to clear it.\nClaims automatically extend to the server's configured height range for the dimension. The system will auto-detect if your selection is inside, around, or on the border of an existing claim, for sub-claims, expanding, or extending.
jm_at.cl.help_viewer=§9§lClaim Viewer§r\nHold in your offhand to see claim info on the action bar. Crouch while holding it to show claim boundaries with particles (20-block range).
