jm_at.kits.info_player_body=§9§lWhat are kits?§r\nKits are bundles of items you can receive. Open this menu (from the Kits section of your Player Tool) to see the kits available to you.\n\n§9§lClaiming a kit§r\nPick a kit to see its contents, then tap §lClaim Kit§r. You need enough free inventory space. If you don't, nothing is taken, so make room and try again.\n\n§9§lTypes§r\n• §lStarter§r — given automatically the first time you join.\n• §lClaimable§r — claimed from this menu. Some can be claimed only §lonce§r; others are §lrepeatable§r after a cooldown.\n\n§9§lStatus labels§r\nEach kit shows its status beside the name:\n• §aAvailable§r — ready to claim now.\n• §eOn cooldown§r — claim again once the timer runs out.\n• §7Already claimed§r — a once-only kit you've received.\n• §7Unlocks at …§r — needs more playtime (or a rank) before it opens.\n\n§9§lWho can claim§r\nSome kits are limited to staff or a specific rank, and some require a minimum playtime before they unlock. Keep playing and more may become available.\n\n§9§lWhere to manage§r\n§8(Staff)§r Create and edit kits with the §2Kit Editor§r (the craftable Kit Tool). It has its own §lKit Info§r guide with full details.
jm_at.kits.info_staff_body=§9§lCreating a kit§r\nOpen the §2Kit Editor§r (the craftable Kit Tool) → §lCreate Kit§r. You can have up to §f%1$s§r kits.\n\n§9§l1. Name§r\nChoose a name and an optional color. Names must be unique (ignoring color).\n\n§9§l2. Pick items§r\nThe kit is built from §lyour own inventory§r — put the items you want in your inventory first, then check the ones to include (up to §f%2$s§r). Items marked §e⚠§r have data (potions, written books, banners, shulker contents, etc.) that can't be fully saved and will be given in a basic form.\n\n§9§l3. Amounts§r\nSet a whole-number amount for each item. The kit's total across all items can't exceed §f%3$s§r (a full inventory).\n\n§9§l4. Options§r\n• §lType§r — §lClaimable§r (grabbed from the Player Tool) or §lStarter§r (auto-given on first join).\n• §lRepeatable§r — off = give once; on = claimable again after a §lcooldown§r (e.g. 30m, 6h, 1d).\n• §lMax total claims§r — for repeatable kits, cap how many times each player can ever claim it (blank/0 = unlimited).\n• §lWho can claim§r — everyone, staff only, or a specific rank.\n• §lMin playtime§r — require a custom time (e.g. 10h), or a playtime rank when Playtime Ranks are on (claimable once a player reaches it, and above). Claimable kits only; Starter kits can't have a playtime requirement.\n• §lVisibility§r — for rank/playtime-gated kits: §lHidden until unlocked§r (default; players don't see it until they qualify) or §lShow locked§r (appears grayed-out with its unlock requirement). Cooldowns are never hidden.\n• §lStarter back-fill§r — also give a Starter kit to existing players who never received it.\n\n§9§lManaging a kit§r\nFrom a kit's page you can §lTest Claim§r (get the items now), §lGive to Player§r (hand it to someone online), §lEdit Settings§r, §lEdit Items§r (re-pick the contents), §lChange Icon§r, §lPin to Top§r (feature it), §lReset Claims§r (clear one player or everyone), or §lDelete§r it.\n§8Tip:§r changing a kit's claim type or limit offers to reset its claim history so the new rules apply cleanly.\n\n§9§lHow players claim§r\nPlayers claim kits from the §lKits§r section of their §2Player Tool§r. The Kit Tool (Kit Editor) is staff-only. Players never use it to claim.\n\n§9§lGive via command§r\nA kit's page has a §lGive via Command§r button with ready-to-use §l/scriptevent§r commands to give or claim the kit — from chat, an NPC, or a command block.
