jm_at.infoa.claims_body=§9§lLand Claims — Admin§r\n\n§2§lClaim Tool§r  (§8jm_at:claim_wand§r)\nSelect two corners to define a claim area. Crouch + hit a block to set corner 1, then crouch + interact to set corner 2. A marker appears at each picked corner so the pending selection is visible. Use the Claim Tool to open the claims menu and confirm the claim.\n\n───────────────────\n§2§lClaim Viewer§r  (§8jm_at:claim_viewer§r)\nHighlights claim boundaries with particles. Works for any nearby claim.\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lAdmin Claims§r\nAdmins can create §9Admin Claims§r — server-owned protected areas that don't count against any player's budget. Useful for spawn, shops, arenas, or other shared builds.\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lOwner-Only Claims§r\nOnly the §9Server Owner§r can create these (a toggle shown when confirming a claim). They're completely private — no other admin or moderator can enter, build, open containers, view or change settings, expand, or even delete them, and they don't appear in the admin claim lists. Use them for sensitive builds only the owner should touch.\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lStaff Access & Bypass§r\nTwo privileges control how staff interact with claims they don't belong to:\n• §6Claim Bypass§r — override protections in regular players' claims.\n• §6Admin Claim Bypass§r — override another admin's claims. Admins always keep access to shared Admin Claims; with this off, an admin acts as a normal player inside another admin's personal claim (unless trusted/added to it). Owner-Only claims ignore both bypasses.\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lBrowse All Claims§r\nView every claim on the server. Filter by player name to find specific claims. From here you can inspect, edit protections, rename, transfer ownership, adjust height, manage sub-claims, or force-delete.\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lClaim Settings§r\n• §6Claims Config§r — max claims per player, starting area, earning rate, dimension restrictions\n• §6Claim Defaults§r — default protections applied to new claims\n• §6Player Abilities§r — control which protections players can toggle themselves\n• §6Default Claim Height§r — set the default Y range per dimension\n• §6Mob Black/Whitelist§r — specific mob types always removed or always allowed in claims\n\n───────────────────\n§2§lClaim amounts and budgets§r\nPlayer budgets are measured in chunks. §81 chunk = 16×16 = 256 blocks of XZ claim area.§r\nWhile the budget is measured in chunks, claims can be any shape and size, and the cost is based on the total area in blocks. For example, a 16×16 claim costs 1 chunk, while a 20×20 claim costs about 1.56 chunks.\n%1$s\n• Starting budget: %2$s chunks\n• Earned budget: +%3$s chunks every %4$s min of tracked playtime\n• Budget formula: min(start + earned + bonus chunks, max + bonus chunks)\n• Base budget cap: %5$s chunks before bonus chunks\n• Expansions and extensions use the same budget; sub-claims do not cost extra budget\n• Admin claims never use player budget but they do show the name of the Admin who created them\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lAdd/Remove Chunks§r\nGrant or remove bonus claim chunks for individual players. Useful for rewards, compensation, or admin overrides.\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lClaim Event Log§r\nAll claim events (creation, deletion, transfers, protection changes, member/rank additions, removals & expirations) are logged with timestamps and player names.\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lProtections§r\nEach claim can toggle up to 13 protections:\n• §6Blocks§r — prevent breaking and placing blocks\n• §6Containers§r — lock chests, barrels, hoppers, etc.\n• §6Entities (mobs)§r — protect mobs and armor stands\n• §6PvP§r — block player-vs-player combat\n• §6Interactions§r — restrict doors, buttons, levers, trapdoors & gates\n• §6Item Use§r — block buckets, flint & steel, bone meal, etc.\n• §6Explosions§r — prevent TNT and creeper damage\n• §6Hostile Mobs§r — block hostile mob spawning inside the claim (also enforces the global Mob Black/Whitelist)\n• §6Crop Trampling§r — protect farmland from being trampled\n• §6Fire Spread§r — prevent fire from spreading within the claim\n• §6Ender Pearls§r — block ender pearl entry into the claim\n• §6Eject Untrusted Players§r — automatically teleport non-members out of the claim\n• §6Allow Vehicle Use§r — exempt minecarts, boats, and other vehicles from entity protection\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lSub-claims§r\nSub-claims are zones inside a parent claim with independent protections and members. Players (or admins) create them using the Claim Tool inside an existing claim. Sub-claims can be nested up to two levels deep (e.g. city → district → house). Deleting a sub-claim that contains nested sub-claims will delete them as well.\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lMembers & Trusted Ranks§r\nClaim owners can add individual members or trust entire server ranks. Both support four roles:\n• §6Visitor:§r can enter the claim only\n• §6Member:§r can interact (doors, buttons, levers)\n• §6Builder:§r full access\n• §6Co-owner:§r full access and can edit claim settings\nBoth members and trusted ranks can be given temporary access that expires automatically.
