jm_at.infoa.server_body_1=§9§lControl Panel§r\n• Server: %1$s§r  •  Whitelist: %2$s\n• Nether: %3$s  •  End: %4$s\n\n§7§lSub-sections:§r\n• §6Config Editor§r — homes, teleport, warn threshold, deathback, AFK\n• §6Item Watch§r — auto-remove banned items or set threshold alerts on tracked items\n• §6Staff & Permissions§r — Mod Privileges, plus Admin Privileges for the owner\n• §6Menu Visibility§r — show/hide player-menu features, and (owner) hide admin-panel buttons\n• §6Ticket Settings§r — open/close ticketing, categories, cooldowns, limits, auto-delete\n• §6Dimension Locks§r — toggle Nether/End access instantly or schedule locks/unlocks\n• §6Server Controls§r — server lock and whitelist management\n• §6Restore Holograms§r — recover despawned hologram entities §8(admin only)§r\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lPlayer Tool Settings§r\n
jm_at.infoa.server_body_2=• Homes: %1$s (max §2%2$s§r)\n• TPA: %3$s (delay §2%4$s§r)\n• Deathback: %5$s\n• AFK detection: %6$s
jm_at.infoa.server_body_3=\n• Gamemode access: %1$s\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lCommands§r\nSave and run custom admin commands. Supports one-time and repeating commands.\n§8Note: some commands require cheats enabled on the world.§r\n\n§9§lGame Commands§r\nNo-typing shortcuts in the Commands panel: your own gamemode, weather (Clear/Rain/Thunder + lock), time (Day/Night/Noon/Midnight + lock), difficulty, world spawn (set or go to), common game rules, and Clear Dropped Items.\n§8Weather/Time/Difficulty/Worldspawn/Clear items need the Game Commands privilege; the Game Rules picker needs the Game Rules privilege; gamemode uses the existing Gamemode privilege. While Gravestones is on, keepInventory stays locked on.§r\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lWarps§r\nCreate and remove server-wide teleport points (up to §250§r).\n• Set each warp's visibility: §lPublic§r, §lStaff-only§r, or §lAdmin-only§r\n• Pin important warps to the top of the list, and Reorder them\n• Hide or show the whole Warps section in the Player Menu\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lCustomize Menu§r\nEach admin can personalize their own panel independently.\n• Show or hide optional top-level buttons on your admin panel\n• Promote sub-menu actions as shortcuts directly on your main page\n§8Path: Admin Tool -> Admin Panel -> Customize Menu§r\n\n───────────────────\n§9§lMenu Visibility§r\nOne screen to control what shows in the menus. Toggle which player features appear in the Player Menu (Tickets/Warnings, Homes, Teleport, Deathback, Warps, Kits) — each staff member sees the toggles for the features they manage. The §9Server Owner§r also gets a section to hide optional top-level admin-panel buttons server-wide.\n§8Path: Admin Tool -> Admin Panel -> Control Panel -> Menu Visibility§r
