## [tx] admins can); keep the two trailing \n.
jm_at.infop.cl_admin_managed=§c§lClaims are admin-managed on this server.§r\n\n
jm_at.infop.cl_body_1=§9§lLand Claims§r\nLand claims are managed using the §2Claim Tool§r (§8jm_at:claim_wand§r).\n\nMore admin-specific info is available in the Admin Tool info pages.\n\n§9§lClaim Tool§r\n§l1.§r §2Crouch + Hit§r a block to set §lCorner 1§r.\n§l2.§r §2Crouch + Interact§r on a block to set §lCorner 2§r.\n§l3.§r Open the Claims menu and tap §lConfirm Pending Claim§r.\nA marker appears at each corner you pick so you can see your pending selection before confirming; tap §lCancel Claim§r to clear it.\nClaims automatically extend to the server's configured height range for the dimension. If your selection sits inside, around, or on the border of an existing claim, it's auto-detected for sub-claims, expanding, or extending.\n\n§9§lClaim Viewer§r  (§8jm_at:claim_viewer§r)\nHold in your offhand to see claim info on the action bar. Crouch while holding it to show claim boundaries with particles (20-block range).\n\n
jm_at.infop.cl_body_2=§8Admins may also configure a Mob Black/Whitelist: specific mob types always removed or always allowed in claims.§r\n\n§9§lMembers§r\nAdd players to your claim with a role:\n• §lVisitor§r — can enter the claim but cannot interact\n• §lMember§r — can use doors, buttons, and levers\n• §lBuilder§r — full access to build and interact\n• §lCo-owner§r — can manage the claim (add members, change settings, create sub-claims)\nMembers can be temporary (15 min to 7 days) or permanent.\n\n§9§lTrusted Ranks§r\nTrust a server rank to give all players with that rank access to your claim. Each trusted rank has a role (visitor, member, builder, or co-owner) and can be set to expire. Useful for granting access to groups without adding players individually.\n\n§9§lExpand & Extend§r\n• §6Expand§r — select a larger area that fully encompasses your claim to grow it in place. Expanding an extended claim will merge it into one rectangle and reset your extensions.\n• §6Extend§r — select an area that borders your claim to attach an extension (up to 2 per claim). Extensions share the same protections and members as the main claim.\n\n§9§lSub-claims§r\nSelect an area inside an existing claim to create a sub-claim with its own protections and members. Up to %1$s sub-claims per claim. Sub-claims can be nested up to two levels deep (e.g. city → district → house).
jm_at.infop.cl_budget=§9§lYour Budget§r\n• Claims: %1$s/%2$s\n• Area used: %3$s/%4$s chunks\n• Chunks earned per §2%6$s§r min of playtime: §2%5$s§r\n• Starting budget: %7$s chunks  •  Max budget: %8$s chunks\n\n
jm_at.infop.cl_dimensions=§9§lDimensions§r\n• Nether: %1$s§r  •  End: %2$s§r\n\n§9§lProtections§r\nNew claims use the server's default protections. You can toggle:\n
jm_at.infop.cl_owner_only=\n\n§9§lOwner-Only Claims§r\nAs the Server Owner you can mark a new claim §4Owner-Only§r when confirming it, making it completely private: no other admin or moderator can enter, build, open containers, view or change its settings, expand, or even delete it, and it's hidden from the admin claim lists.
